  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Use the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(1+x)^{7}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(1.05)^{7}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n$(1.05)^{7}\u2248$ \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that when $n$ is a positive integer, \n\n$$\n(1+x)^{n}=1+nx+\\frac{1}{2!}n(n-1){x}^{2}+\u22ef+{x}^{n}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(1+x)}^{7} & =1+7x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 6\\cdot {x}^{2}+\u22ef+{x}^{7} \\\\  & =1+7x+21{x}^{2}+\u22ef+{x}^{7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n{(1+x)}^{7}\u22481+7x+21{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=0.05$ into the above approximation of $(1+x)^{7}:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1.05)^{7} & =(1+0.05)^{7} \\\\  & \u22481+7(0.05)+21(0.05)^{2} \\\\  & =1+7(0.05)+21(0.002\\,5) \\\\  & =1+0.35+0.052\\,5 \\\\  & \u22481.403,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
